🔁 Reconciliation Flow – Sequence Overview

1️⃣ Trigger
	•	A scheduler or background service periodically initiates the reconciliation cycle (for example, every few minutes).
	•	The trigger ensures continuous alignment between Redis runtime state and metadata persistence layer (such as DB or service registry).

⸻

2️⃣ Fetch Current States
	•	The reconciler fetches:
	•	Active nodes list from Redis (contains heartbeat timestamps, container IDs, and status).
	•	Expected nodes/tasks metadata from the metadata service or internal store (representing the system’s authoritative view).

⸻

3️⃣ State Comparison & Mismatch Detection
	•	The reconciliation engine performs pairwise validation to detect:
	•	Orphaned tasks: Task assigned to a node that is missing or inactive in Redis.
	•	Stale node registrations: Node entry in Redis with no corresponding metadata record.
	•	Duplicate or inconsistent entries: Task or node recorded with conflicting states (e.g., RUNNING vs COMPLETED).
	•	Heartbeat expiry: Node last seen beyond TTL threshold (considered offline).

⸻

4️⃣ Healing and Corrective Actions
Depending on the mismatch type, corrective actions are executed:

Mismatch Type                           Resolution Action
Orphaned Task               Reassign or terminate the task, and update metadata
Stale Node                  Remove the entry from Redis registry
Duplicated State            Keep the latest or authoritative copy, clean others
Expired Heartbeat           Mark node as inactive and reallocate its tasks

These updates are performed atomically to avoid race conditions during parallel reconciliation runs.

⸻

5️⃣ Metadata Synchronization
	•	The reconciler updates both Redis and metadata service to reflect the corrected state.
	•	Changes propagate via internal event streams (Kafka / messaging layer) to ensure other system components are notified of corrections.

⸻

6️⃣ Logging, Metrics, and Monitoring
	•	Each reconciliation cycle logs:
	•	Start and end timestamps
	•	Number of inconsistencies detected and resolved
	•	Duration and latency per reconciliation step
	•	Metrics are published to Prometheus / internal observability dashboards, enabling tracking of reconciliation health and trends.

